WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.602
-Thank you for being
such a good sport.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.770
Every time you come on the show,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.338
we do a little dance-off,
and you always crush me.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.339
-That's not true.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.507
-I just love to see
your moves, man.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.507
You know I'm a fan.
-Thank you. It's a blast.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:09.509
It's a workout, too.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.776
-Trust me --
I just caught my breath.

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:12.145
-Personal training.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.812
-The audience knows, but during
the commercial break,

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:17.116
yeah, they came out with
an oxygen tank, and it was sad.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:18.985
It was really sad.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.820
-Why do I actually believe it?

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.521
-Yeah, it did happen, yeah.

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:23.956
I got to congratulate you,
I think.

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.092
Yesterday was your anniversary?

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.027
-One of them. So...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.963
-Happy anniversary.
With your girlfriend? What...

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:33.499
-Yeah. So, my
girlfriend and I --

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:38.204
You know, Ky asked me to be the
girlfriend on the 8th.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.639
January 8th.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.307
But then, I was like,
"You know what?

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.010
I also need to ask
you to be my girlfriend."

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.678
So we did that.
-Okay.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.848
-And yesterday was the
anniversary of that day,

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.450
when I asked Ky
to be my girlfriend.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.318
We actually celebrate
four days, though --

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.687
when Ky asked me
to be girlfriend,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.689
when I asked Ky
to be girlfriend,

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.859
when we told each other that
we liked each other,

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.360
and when we kissed
for the first time.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.362
-Ah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.530
-Yeah!

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:10.536
We celebrate all four --
8th, 14th, 28th, and 29th.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:13.039
-Is that exhausting?

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.907
-I mean, we're on
month number eight now.

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:15.975
-So it's cute.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.343
-And we'll probably
stop at a year.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.046
I would imagine, every year,
we would only celebrate.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:23.416
-I notice you're not wearing
your signature hair bow.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.285
My girls wear them all the time.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.353
You have JoJo dolls.
You have your own clothing line.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.621
I mean, it's --
-I got it all.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.922
-Yeah, bud.
-Crazy. It's amazing.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.691
-I'm so happy. Yeah, you do.
You do have it all, yeah.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:35.494
-It is. It's wild.
It's so awesome.

00:01:35.494 --> 00:01:38.130
You know, I'm so thankful
for everything that I have.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.366
Being a brand
is the coolest thing ever.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.501
-Yeah. I think you handle it
so well, too.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.437
-Thank you. I appreciate it.
-I really do, yeah. Respect.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.538
-Thank you. I'm a human brand.

00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:47.873
-Yeah, you are.
-So it's fun.

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:51.110
-You are a human brand. Yeah.
But this is even crazier.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.945
They want to rename
Ronald Reagan Airport to

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:54.513
JoJo Siwa
Washington National Airport.

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.615
-They do!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.616
-Look at this.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.618
Change.org.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.421
Go to this Website.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.989
-Go petition.
-You're really close.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.223
This might happen.

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.692
-When my mom told me,
I was like, "Oh, funny.

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:09.895
Like, ha-ha.
500 petitions, right?"

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:13.466
77,398.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.466
-That's a lot!

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:15.668
-That is a lot.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.070
If you get to 150,000,
this is going to be --

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.305
This is going to happen.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.107
-Is that how that works,
if it actually gets there?

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.408
-I don't know how things
work in life,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.309
but I think this is how it does.

00:02:24.309 --> 00:02:27.947
-No, it becomes one of the top
signed on the website.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.482
That's cool!
-Yes, of course!

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.917
-Yeah!

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.752
-When you come on next time,
you'll have your own airport.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.086
-I am going to
have my own airport, yes.

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:36.522
-And you will be the champ on
"Dancing with the Stars."

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:39.158
I'm rooting for you, buddy.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.393
[ Cheers and applause ]
-This is major.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.427
-Thank you.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.595
-I think you're
going to be great.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.664
-Thank you. I'm so excited.
-Are you nervous?

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.099
-Not really.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.367
I told myself after "Dance Moms"
that I was never allowed to be

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.270
nervous again,
and I stuck to that, actually,

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.472
because I miss out on the fun
if I'm always nervous.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:57.276
But being in rehearsals,
it is so hard,

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:58.443
and everyone's like,
"Well, you're a dancer,

00:02:58.443 --> 00:02:59.612
so you got it, right?"

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.181
And I'm like, "Yes,"
but I explain it like

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:04.283
a football player
trying to play baseball.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.284
It's still a sport.

00:03:05.284 --> 00:03:06.285
It's just
a really different sport.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.286
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.520
-And that's how it is.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.155
You know, the styles
I'm trained in for dancing

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:11.858
are very different
than everything ballroom.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.659
But it's so fun.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.328
My partner is a female.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.829
I'm the first-ever
same-sex couple on

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.830
"Dancing with the Stars."

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.831
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.232
Yeah.
-I love that.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.468
-Thank you.
So, it's really cool.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.437
And we're both so comfortable
with the idea.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.172
She's incredible, so talented.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.408
I can't wait!
Monday, Monday, Monday, Monday!

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:31.777
-You did me a solid.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.213
You were one of the first guests
on "The Kids Tonight Show,"

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:37.183
which is going to stream
October 14th on Peacock.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.984
We started a show just for kids,

00:03:38.984 --> 00:03:40.520
and you were one of
the first guests.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.854
So thank you for doing that.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.890
-It's the most fun show
ever, no offense.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.891
But it's...

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.092
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:48.361
-But they're cute, right?

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.763
-They're so fun and cute
and just little,

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.464
and they know what
they're talking about

00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:54.567
and they're well put-together
and they're creative.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.935
And we played games,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.603
and they whupped me
at all of them.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:59.272
But they're just awesome.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.207
-I want to talk about
"The J Team."

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.842
-Oh, yeah!
-That's me, man.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.177
We're on the J Team together.
-Yeah, you're on the J Team.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.611
-I know! Yeah, "J."
JoJo, Jimmy.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:07.012
Yeah, we're on the J Team.

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:08.781
-You were the first person
that I told about the J Team,

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.283
so, literally, you are.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:13.419
-I am the original.
I'm the O.G. J.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.954
-O.G. J.
-I'm the O.G. J.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.889
-Yeah, you are.
-The O.G. J.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.024
And let's talk about
"The J Team.

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:21.127
Now, this is on Paramount+
streaming on this.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.561
Tell everyone what it's about.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.463
-So "The J Team" --
I like to explain it as if

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:28.434
it's me, but I'm a completely
normal 14-year-old.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.169
But I still act the same,
dress the same,

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.770
I am the same,
but I'm just normal.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.605
I go to my dance studio.

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:35.642
My dance studio gets turned over
to new management.

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.075
New management
kicks me off the team.

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:38.076
It's really dramatic.

00:04:38.076 --> 00:04:39.545
So I make my own team.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.782
And my own team is made up
of gymnasts and soccer players

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.750
and football players
and cheerleaders

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.219
and, you know,
people who don't really fit in.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:50.756
But they can, because you --
Everybody fits in, in a way.

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:53.426
So it's all about
being yourself,

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:56.328
letting nobody change you,
staying true to who you are,

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:57.897
and not giving up

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.065
because somebody
tries to make you give up.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:01.734
-There you go. That's it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.269
I love that message.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.870
"The J Team" --
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.539
Here is JoJo Siwa in
"The J Team."

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:08.907
Take a look.
-Yeah!

